# Work in progress — on this Mac only.
#
# The hazard is publishing, not deploying, and it is worth being exact about
# which: this repo is public on GitHub, so a commit is a publication of its
# own, and unfinished design does not belong there.
#
# The 6:45 Dispatch run does NOT ship whatever happens to be sitting in
# public/. publish() in scripts/dispatch/run.py deploys from a throwaway
# worktree of HEAD with only the Dispatch's own files laid over it, precisely
# so that an unfinished page cannot ride along — which it did, twice, before
# that was built. So the thing to be careful about is committing to public/,
# not editing it: a commit is what puts work on the live site the next
# morning. preview/ sits outside public/ anyway, which keeps both honest.
preview/

# The Dispatch's own pages are generated every morning and deliberately not
# kept. prune() holds six mornings on disk and deletes the rest; git is a
# history rather than a folder, so committing them would keep every edition
# that prune had already thrown away, for ever, in a public repo. They are
# deployed from disk by publish(), so nothing here needs them to be tracked.
public/dispatch.html
public/dispatch/
